    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0460" n="344" xml:id="pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/520.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Dominican Republic to the Secretary of
                            State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Dominican Government informs me that Horacio Vásquez<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d495-f1"/> and the two Rodriguez left Porto Rico today for Cuba,
                    bound for Haiti, and that Vásquez will receive from the United States via Cape
                    Haitien 500,000 rounds and 1000 rifles.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
